{# Not a macro — a whole manifest. `k8s/manifests` renders this file as `ingressroute.yaml`
   for every role that names `ingressroute.yaml` in its `manifests_files` and ships no
   `templates/ingressroute.yaml.j2` of its own (`manifests_shared_defaults` in that role's
   defaults). 16 roles' IngressRoute templates were byte-identical wrappers around the
   `ingressroute()` macro below; this file is that wrapper, rendered once (#3043).

   THE ENTRY IS THE INPUT. Name, host label, port and Authelia gate all come from the role's
   `containers_list` entry, which is also where the deploy derives the role's traefik ordering
   edge from (`ansible/filter_plugins/toposort.py:build_k8s_dep_map`) — a hostname on the entry
   is what says "this role is routed", now that the route itself leaves no file in the role.

   A role whose route needs anything else — extra middlewares, a second hostname, the
   public-route opt-out, a bypass prefix, a Jinja condition — keeps its own
   `templates/ingressroute.yaml.j2`, which wins over this file. The macro header in
   `ansible/templates/ingressroute.yml.j2` lists every parameter such a role would reach for. #}
{% from 'ingressroute.yml.j2' import ingressroute with context %}
---
{{ ingressroute(
    container_item.name,
    container_item.hostname | default(container_item.name),
    container_item.port,
    container_item.use_authelia,
  )
}}
